{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Service Level Objectives, control-plane, queue, runner and telemetry health from agentsfleetd. Panels 20-25 are the SLO view; everything below panel 4 is the operator view.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Service Level Indicator (SLI). Good events: admissions the queue accepted (`appended`) or recognised as an idempotent repeat (`replayed`). Valid events exclude `over_budget`, which is the deployment refusing work on purpose rather than failing at it. Target 99% — a starting threshold, not a measured objective; see docs/architecture/observability.md §Service Level Objectives. Reads 100% when nothing has been admitted, because nothing has failed.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 20,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "1 - ((sum(increase(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"deferred|refused\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(increase(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)), 1))",
          "legendFormat": "availability",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SLO · Admission availability",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "SLI. Good events: runs a runner finished with a result (`processed`). Valid events: every finished run — the outcome set is closed at `processed` and `fleet_error`, and a failure moves both this family and agentsfleet_runner_failures_total, so the two agree by construction. Target 95% — a starting threshold. Reads 100% on an idle window.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.95
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 21,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "1 - ((sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total{outcome=\"fleet_error\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total[$__range])) or vector(0)), 1))",
          "legendFormat": "success",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SLO · Runner success rate",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "SLI. The fraction of samples where the oldest unconfirmed admission is younger than the replay floor. The floor is derived from source at apply time (MIN_AGE + INTERVAL in rustd/crates/afd_runner/src/sweep/replay.rs), never typed here: a row younger than MIN_AGE is deliberately left for its own producer, and one older than that should be gone within one sweeper pass. Past the floor means the sweeper is not keeping up. Target 99%.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 22,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "avg_over_time((max(agentsfleet_admission_backlog_oldest_age_seconds) < bool __ADMISSION_REPLAY_FLOOR_SECONDS__)[$__range:1m]) or vector(1)",
          "legendFormat": "within floor",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SLO · Work picked up inside the replay floor",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Seconds since the most overdue runner was last heard from. The family reports a Unix epoch (rustd/crates/afd_observability/src/runner.rs — last_seen_ms / MILLIS_PER_SECOND), so every reader subtracts it from evaluation time; plotting it raw renders tens of thousands of years. Red at the source-derived offline threshold, which is what the runner-silent rule compares against. The aggregation is min-by-runner, not a bare max: the per-runner table is in-process and never evicted, so a runner that heartbeats to one daemon replica leaves a frozen reading on every other replica. Live proof at authoring — runner 019fec54 read 9 s on the replica serving it and 1178 s on its sibling. The freshest observation is the one that is true, because any replica hearing from a runner proves the runner is alive.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": "__RUNNER_OFFLINE_SECONDS_NUM__"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 23,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(min by (runner_id) (time() - agentsfleet_runner_last_seen_seconds)) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "worst age",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Worst runner heartbeat age",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "UNPROVEN — this deployment has served tens of events, not weeks of them. At the time this panel shipped the whole history was 14 admissions and 10 runner executions, so the burn rate below is arithmetic over a sample too small to set an objective from. Read the shape, not the number, until the windows are full. Google Site Reliability Engineering workbook shape: burn rate is the error ratio divided by the error budget (1 - target). Two windows per severity — the long window makes the budget claim and the short window resets it, so a burn that has already stopped does not keep paging. Page when 1h AND 5m both exceed 14.4 (2% of a 30-day budget in an hour); open a ticket when 6h AND 30m both exceed 6.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 24,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"deferred|refused\"}[1h])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[1h])) or vector(0)), 1e-9)) / 0.01",
          "legendFormat": "1h burn",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"deferred|refused\"}[5m])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[5m])) or vector(0)), 1e-9)) / 0.01",
          "legendFormat": "5m burn",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"deferred|refused\"}[6h])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[6h])) or vector(0)), 1e-9)) / 0.01",
          "legendFormat": "6h burn",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"deferred|refused\"}[30m])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(rate(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[30m])) or vector(0)), 1e-9)) / 0.01",
          "legendFormat": "30m burn",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Error budget burn — admission availability (unproven)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
