        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### What this dashboard cannot show you, and why\n\nTwelve families are declared in `docs/metrics.census.tsv` and have **no producer** in this build.\nThe ledger is `rustd/crates/afd_observability/src/metrics/produced.rs`; each line below quotes its\nreason. A gap is on this screen rather than in a document because the families an operator reaches\nfor first at 3am are two of the ones that are missing.\n\n| Family | Why nothing feeds it |\n|---|---|\n| `agentsfleet_fleet_triggered_total` | the daemon this ports declares the family and increments it nowhere |\n| `agentsfleet.telemetry.samples_dropped` | the ring it counted belongs to the daemon being replaced |\n| `agentsfleet_otlp_queue_depth` | the software development kit owns the export queue and exposes no depth |\n| `agentsfleet_repair_production_to_queue_seconds` | the repair-result ingress has no Rust home yet |\n| `agentsfleet_repair_queue_to_completion_seconds` | the repair-result ingress has no Rust home yet |\n| `agentsfleet_repair_provider_results_total` | the repair-result ingress has no Rust home yet |\n| `agentsfleet_repair_correlations_total` | the repair-result ingress has no Rust home yet |\n| `agentsfleet_repair_verification_intents_created_total` | the repair-result ingress has no Rust home yet |\n| `agentsfleet_account_teardown_unregister_failures_total` | account teardown is declared unported |\n| `agentsfleet_http_trace_suppressed_total` | every matched request is traced, so nothing is suppressed to count |\n| `agentsfleet_library_cache_outcome_total` | the revision-keyed response cache is a declared non-port |\n| `agentsfleet_library_pool_result_total` | the acquire happens inside the store, where the read path cannot see how it ended |\n\n**Two Service Level Indicators are therefore impossible, not merely empty.** End-to-end fleet\navailability — was a fleet that was asked for actually started — has no denominator\n(`agentsfleet_fleet_triggered_total` is never incremented) and no numerator (no family counts a\nstart). Repair latency has no histogram. Neither is a threshold waiting to be tuned; both need a\nfamily that does not exist, and a new family is a new census row and its own milestone.\n\nThere is also **no HTTP request-duration histogram anywhere in the census**, so the most standard\nService Level Indicator of all — API latency — cannot be drawn here at any target.\n\n### This dashboard is development-only by accident, not by design\n\nDevelopment and production resolve to the **same Grafana stack, the same namespace, the same\nPrometheus datasource and the same ingest credential**, and no series carries a\n`deployment.environment` attribute — the daemon's resource is service name, namespace, version and\nan optional instance identifier, and nothing else. Today every series here is development because\nthe production Fly application runs zero machines. **The day production deploys, every panel above\nsilently sums both environments and no query can separate them.** Emitting\n`deployment.environment` is the named blocker on that deploy.\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "targets": [],
      "title": "Declared gaps · what this dashboard cannot show",
      "type": "text"
    }
